E = {
    15: "The eyes of Satan’s… They mistakenly blink once, and the marionettes turn their heads, all winding their necks together at the same time, to look at Satan. They watch Satan. These dolls are blinkless, smiling jesters, yet scrutinizing with dead eyes. Souls conformed by the pressure, the pressure birthing deformity in this exile worse than hell. ",
    36: "The dolls all spring up one foot with the next, marching closer. Their joy in the ignorance, toying with death in depravity of jestered joys. They encircle Satan, their eyes beaming down at his body on the floor, the light and yellow shining off and across their fake faces and hair, showing the rigidity of their lessons strained into them, until they obey as they do now, seeming older than time. ",
    44: "The doll behind now puts the grip of one hand at one side of the cheek, and another hand at the other side of the mouth, ripping his lips apart by force. Another stands in front, with stubby but skinny toy proportions, and this dark-haired porcelain boy in overalls, with rosy cheeks, smiles in a joy likened unto a child-predator, where he has found a scared little one alone, that being this frowny small Satan… He forces Satan’s teeth, prying them apart by tiny fake fingers, as Satan’s tears and cries continue. Satan is dehumanized, without consideration of his suffering, and his movement speaks of a “No, don’t.”  ",
    46: "The toy boy grabs the gums and fleshy gum-tooth, which there are many of. He takes them off the floor in scoops, forcing them into Satan’s mouth, past the forced-open teeth and mouth. Satan’s face recoils backwards, but another small one is holding his head now, so he cannot take his head away from this. What they want him to eat is now mixed with hairs and carpet fibers from the floor. The boy’s eyes grow darker in soul as the grin stretches harder, his eyes and cheeks shining with a sickly yellow reflected. Satan tastes the flesh, and it is of a sickly sweetness, of a flesh ridden with some disease unknown. ",
    52: "Satan chews on the fleshy sweet rot of gummy thick flesh that was once his teeth, now convulsing in shivers of disgust at the face, like a child who can’t stand the taste of vegetables. Satan is sad and frowning, still crying. The mouth is still held open, as little toys caress and pat his hair. The black-haired, rosy-cheeked boy is in a wide-open gaze from eyelids peeled back from excitement’s ease, staring without break from Satan’s weeping sorrow. This black-haired boy is grinning so hard that it hurts to look at. ",
    60: "Eventually, all of them get up and leave, even in the vision where he is above them, and they are gone. Walking away like little tiny humans in puppet and doll forms, it is too disturbing in its uncanniness every time. ",
    64: "The head and skull burning, burning. Scalding skull. Pins and needles in the hands and feet. Ringing louder now. Distant. The heart beating louder. The heart is drumming fast. Pins and needles still stabbing him. Stabbing at the ears precisely. It is faster now, all faster. The pupils his own grow large with a drooling taking on. The weight of Leviathan sits on his chest. The teeth fall out of his mouth. Cold and dry throat. The floor under his head is stabbing at the ear more so now, big and small in sharpness. Nerves known by location in their fear, and a detached surgical ringing loud alongside growing distance over the body. The heart is firing like a machine gun now. The guts twist up into knots. Satan pisses himself. A flatline sound screaming far away. ",
    68: "He sees this all as he feels it, nothing. Satan sees himself lay his head out limp, dead. The lights in his unblinking corpse still reflecting colors, colors bright with empty, in the darkened corner of this too-much exile. When the head falls limp, Satan sees that it was a pupil of the boy in front again. All of what he thought was his death was felt as himself, but just seen through the eyes of a puppet torturing him. He cannot get out of this prison; that is the greatest feeling then. It is all a game to them. ",
    78: "Deeper the Satan sinks, not through twelve of twelve eternities, but through this: a one followed not by one hundred zeros as eternities, but by ten billion zeros as the number of eternities. That number is then raised to the power of itself, and the result raised to the power of itself again, ten more times in all, until the process reaches an exhaustion of comprehension. Call it the Number. Twelve of twelve eternities, multiplied by the Number: that is how long Satan has already been held in Leviathan’s abyss, and it is only a point in his time there, one over the Number of his whole stay. The whole is longer than that span by the Number again, so the full length of it is twelve of twelve eternities, multiplied by the Number, and multiplied by the Number once more. This stay mentioned is never ending, that limit only being used for reference as a yardstick, so even its total can be multiplied further by the Number.  ",
    89: "— 1 Corinthians 2:9 *Geneva Bible* (1599) ",
}
